# Copyright headers on source files

Every **new** source file must begin with the same GPL copyright header used throughout this repository. When editing existing source that lacks the header, add it.

## Applies to

- Project-authored source: `.py`, `.pyi`, `.pyw`, `.pyx`, shell/PowerShell scripts (`.sh`, `.ps1`, `.bat`), and other first-party code
- Do **not** add this header to vendored/third-party assets (e.g. minified libraries under `molmanager/ui/static/`)

## Required header (Python and `#`-comment languages)

Place at the top of the file. For scripts with a shebang (`#!/usr/bin/env …`), keep the shebang as line 1 and put the header immediately below it.

```
# This file is part of MolManager.
# Copyright (C) 2026 Hunter Picard
#
# MolManager is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify
# it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by
# the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or
# (at your option) any later version.
#
# MolManager is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,
# but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
# MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the
# GNU General Public License for more details.
#
# You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License
# along with MolManager.  If not, see <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.
```

## Checklist for new files

- [ ] Header present (after shebang if any)
- [ ] Blank line after the header before imports/code
- [ ] No Cursor co-author attribution in the file or related commits
